    "body": "Thanks.  I had a typo in my brew command and took that to mean that the package didn't exists there (I assumed for Apple silicon.)\n\n\nAll better now.\n\n\nA\n\n________________________________\nFrom: David Knaack <notifications@github.com>\nSent: Monday, March 1, 2021 11:07:56 AM\nTo: starship/starship\nCc: Alex Lesniak; Author\nSubject: Re: [starship/starship] Request for aarch64-apple-darwin (Apple silicon) (#2394)\n\n        This message originated from outside Trinidad Benham. Please use caution when opening attachments, clicking links, or responding to this email.\n\n\n\nUnless the build will fail, this is already implemented and will be included in the release. For now you can also get binaries from homebrew.\n\n—\nYou are receiving this because you authored the thread.\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/2394#issuecomment-788155467>, or unsubscribe<https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/APGMDWYGI6XBDOYJTTLZJGDTBPJXZANCNFSM4YM7AD6Q>.\nDISCLAIMER: This communication, along with any attachments, is intended only for the use of the addressee and may contain legally privileged and confidential information. If you are not the intended recipient, you are hereby notified that any dissemination, distribution or copying of any information contained in or attached to this communication is strictly prohibited. If you have received this message in error, please notify the sender immediately and destroy the original communication and its attachments.\nP Please consider the impact of printing this email\n\n\nThis message has been scanned for malware by Websense. www.websense.com\n",
